From: Xiang Mei <xmei5@asu.edu>
Subject: [PATCH] fbcon: tileblit: clamp tile_putcs() to the pixmap size

tile_putcs() sizes its staging buffer straight from the number of console
cells it is asked to draw:

	int size = sizeof(u32) * count;
	blit.indices = (u32 *)fb_get_buffer_offset(info, &info->pixmap, size);
	for (i = 0; i < count; i++)
		blit.indices[i] = (u32)(scr_readw(s++) & charmask);

fb_get_buffer_offset() is a bump allocator over info->pixmap: when the
request does not fit in the space left it rewinds to offset 0 and hands
back the buffer base, without checking that the request fits in the
buffer at all.  The default pixmap installed by do_register_framebuffer()
is a kmalloc(FBPIXMAPSIZE) of 8192 bytes, so any count above 2048 writes
past the end of that allocation.

The sibling implementations bit_putcs(), cw_putcs(), ccw_putcs() and
ud_putcs() all cap the per-iteration cell count against info->pixmap.size
and loop; tile_putcs() is the only one that does not.

count is vc->vc_cols, which tracks info->var.xres / vc->vc_font.width.
A 1-pixel-wide font installed with KDFONTOP while the device is still in
a graphics mode stays in effect when the device is switched to tile (text)
mode, so on arkfb and s3fb, whose maximum xres is 4096, count can reach
4096 and the repaint writes 4 * count bytes into the 8192-byte pixmap.
A local user who owns the VT and can open /dev/fbX reaches this:

  BUG: KASAN: slab-out-of-bounds in tile_putcs (drivers/video/fbdev/core/tileblit.c:69)
  Write of size 4 at addr ffff88800c622000 by task exploit/143

  Call Trace:
   tile_putcs (drivers/video/fbdev/core/tileblit.c:69)
   fbcon_putcs (drivers/video/fbdev/core/fbcon.c:1392)
   do_update_region (drivers/tty/vt/vt.c:656)
   redraw_screen (drivers/tty/vt/vt.c:1008)
   fbcon_blank (drivers/video/fbdev/core/fbcon.c:2315)
   do_unblank_screen (drivers/tty/vt/vt.c:4756)
   vt_ioctl (drivers/tty/vt/vt_ioctl.c:743)
   tty_ioctl (drivers/tty/tty_io.c:2792)
   __x64_sys_ioctl (fs/ioctl.c:597)

  Allocated by task 143:
   do_register_framebuffer (drivers/video/fbdev/core/fbmem.c:502)
   register_framebuffer (drivers/video/fbdev/core/fbmem.c:602)
   ark_pci_probe (drivers/video/fbdev/arkfb.c:1051)

  The buggy address belongs to the object at ffff88800c620000
   which belongs to the cache kmalloc-8k of size 8192
  The buggy address is located 0 bytes to the right of
   allocated 8192-byte region [ffff88800c620000, ffff88800c622000)

Chunk the write against info->pixmap.size the way bit_putcs() does.

Fixes: 1da177e4c3f4 ("Linux-2.6.12-rc2")
Reported-by: Weiming Shi <bestswngs@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Xiang Mei <xmei5@asu.edu>
---
--- a/drivers/video/fbdev/core/tileblit.c
+++ b/drivers/video/fbdev/core/tileblit.c
@@ -55,20 +55,33 @@ static void tile_putcs(struct vc_data *v
 {
 	struct fb_tileblit blit;
 	unsigned short charmask = vc->vc_hi_font_mask ? 0x1ff : 0xff;
-	int size = sizeof(u32) * count, i;
+	u32 maxcnt = info->pixmap.size / sizeof(u32);
+	u32 cnt, i;
+
+	if (!maxcnt)
+		return;
 
-	blit.sx = xx;
 	blit.sy = yy;
-	blit.width = count;
 	blit.height = 1;
 	blit.fg = fg;
 	blit.bg = bg;
-	blit.length = count;
-	blit.indices = (u32 *) fb_get_buffer_offset(info, &info->pixmap, size);
-	for (i = 0; i < count; i++)
-		blit.indices[i] = (u32)(scr_readw(s++) & charmask);
 
-	info->tileops->fb_tileblit(info, &blit);
+	while (count) {
+		cnt = min_t(u32, count, maxcnt);
+
+		blit.sx = xx;
+		blit.width = cnt;
+		blit.length = cnt;
+		blit.indices = (u32 *)fb_get_buffer_offset(info, &info->pixmap,
+							  cnt * sizeof(u32));
+		for (i = 0; i < cnt; i++)
+			blit.indices[i] = (u32)(scr_readw(s++) & charmask);
+
+		info->tileops->fb_tileblit(info, &blit);
+
+		count -= cnt;
+		xx += cnt;
+	}
 }
 
 static void tile_clear_margins(struct vc_data *vc, struct fb_info *info,
